    erkennung: `The social Eight doesn't secure herself through individual territory like the SE8, but through visible leadership and responsibility for the group: she wants to protect, order, give direction. In my book <em>Enneagramm Zoo</em> I describe the image of the <strong>Lion</strong>, enthroned high on a rock, roaring majestically – its presence fills the space, an emblem of natural authority. It needs its pride, its task, its place at the top.<br><br>Unlike the self-preservation Eight, whose power shows up in her own territory, the SO8's power grows when it becomes visible to others. Anyone who understands this reads her authority not as a hunger for power, but as an expression of the worry about being weak or overlooked – her pride is both a protective shell and an obligation toward those for whom she carries responsibility.`,
